\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {1}{\ignorespaces Script distribution across all 66.9M unique toponyms. IPA coverage percentages reflect successful transcription within the 57.6M training namespace toponyms (gn/wd/tgn). v6 achieves 53.4\% overall IPA coverage (30.8M toponyms) via Epitran extensions (102 language-script pairs), Phonikud (Hebrew), and CharsiuG2P (CJK, Korean). \textsuperscript  {*}Both Hiragana and Katakana have 0\% IPA coverage due to a routing bug (see §\ref  {sec:future-japanese} for details and observed robustness). Overall IPA coverage improved from v5's 50.8\% through extended Epitran support and elimination of AnyAscii romanisation.\relax }}{12}{table.caption.16}\protected@file@percent }
